      "costUsd": 0.005372,
      "pronunciationText": "Last video ended with a goal. You're saving for a holiday, and you want six thousand dollars in two years, from deposits at the end of every month, at six per cent a year, compounded monthly. How much should each deposit be? A quick guess is six thousand divided by twenty-four months, which is two hundred and fifty dollars. Is the real answer more than that, or less? Make a guess."
    },
