      "pronunciationText": "Here, the payments are monthly, so r is zero point zero zero five, and n is twenty-four. Put the goal in for the future value, and M is the unknown. Six thousand equals M, times one point zero zero five to the twenty-four, minus one, over zero point zero zero five. That fraction is about twenty-five point four three, so divide by it. M is two hundred and thirty-five dollars and ninety-two cents, to the nearest cent. That's a little less than the guess, because interest adds about three hundred and thirty-eight dollars. But watch the goal. Two hundred and thirty-five dollars ninety-two reaches only five thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine dollars ninety-one. It falls nine cents short. To be sure of reaching a goal, round up, to two hundred and thirty-five dollars ninety-three."
