      "pronunciationText": "Over a longer time, interest does far more. Say the goal is six hundred thousand dollars in thirty years, at the same rate. Dividing by three hundred and sixty months suggests one thousand, six hundred and sixty-six dollars sixty-seven. But the same steps give five hundred and ninety-seven dollars and thirty cents to the nearest cent, so round up to five hundred and ninety-seven dollars thirty-one. You deposit about two hundred and fifteen thousand dollars, and interest adds about three hundred and eighty-five thousand."
