      "pronunciationText": "Next, a different payment period. Four hundred and fifty dollars goes in at the end of every fortnight, for twenty-five years, at six point four per cent a year, compounded fortnightly. There are twenty-six fortnights in a year, so r is zero point zero six four, divided by twenty-six, and n is twenty-six times twenty-five, which is six hundred and fifty. Keep r as that exact fraction. Rounded to zero point zero zero two four six two, it would add about a hundred and thirty-five dollars after six hundred and fifty periods. The future value is seven hundred and twenty thousand, eight hundred and eighty-five dollars and thirty-two cents."
