      "pronunciationText": "Now the time is the unknown. Back to the holiday, but you can only spare two hundred dollars a month. How many deposits until you reach six thousand? Set six thousand equal to two hundred, times one point zero zero five to the n, minus one, over zero point zero zero five. Rearranging gives one point zero zero five to the n equals one point one five. The unknown is a power, so take logs. n is log one point one five over log one point zero zero five, which is about twenty-eight point zero two. But in this model, the balance only changes at each month's end, when the interest and a deposit go in. After twenty-eight deposits it's five thousand, nine hundred and ninety-four dollars ninety, still short. So round up. It takes twenty-nine deposits."
